From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wmp: Implement what WPF's MediaElement uses.

WPF's MediaPlayer / MediaElement drive the Windows Media Player control
from their own state engine (WpfGfx core/av): every call that fails
ends its state arc and raises MediaFailed, and it waits for player
events before it raises MediaOpened.

Game impacted: Veggie Blast (UNIS, its .NET host) plays its intro movie
(a MediaElement) and its music (a MediaPlayer): the movie failed with
"The method or operation is not implemented" and the music never
started.

- IWMPSettings::put_volume / put_balance: a graph without an audio
  stream (the intro movie) answers E_NOTIMPL from IBasicAudio; that is
  not an error (play() returned E_NOTIMPL).
- IWMPControls::get_isAvailable: answer "play", "pause" and "stop" (any
  media), other items not available instead of E_NOTIMPL.
- IWMPControls::pause: open the graph if needed and pause it,
  wmppsPaused.
- IWMPPlayer4::get_openState / get_playState: the last states sent.
- IWMPSettings rate (IMediaSeeking::SetRate) and balance (IBasicAudio),
  applied when the graph is opened too.
- IWMPControls::put_currentPosition: send PositionChange once the
  position is set. WPF opens media by playing, pausing and seeking to
  0, and waits for this event to finish opening.
- Before rendering the file, ask the client site (IServiceProvider) for
  IWMPGraphCreation and call GraphCreationPreRender / PostRender: WPF
  adds its own EVR, with its presenter, to the graph there.

The graph is now opened by open_graph(), shared by play() and pause();
the duration is read once the graph is opened.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wmp/player.c b/dlls/wmp/player.c
index 583f5847..ccc7ec8c 100644
--- a/dlls/wmp/player.c
+++ b/dlls/wmp/player.c
@@ -42,9 +42,33 @@ static void update_state(WindowsMediaPlayer *wmp, LONG type, LONG state)
     V_VT(params) = VT_UI4;
     V_UI4(params) = state;
 
+    if (type == DISPID_WMPCOREEVENT_OPENSTATECHANGE)
+        wmp->open_state = state;
+    else if (type == DISPID_WMPCOREEVENT_PLAYSTATECHANGE)
+        wmp->play_state = state;
+
     call_sink(wmp->wmpocx, type, &dispparams);
 }
 
+static void position_changed(WindowsMediaPlayer *wmp, double old_position, double new_position)
+{
+    DISPPARAMS dispparams;
+    VARIANTARG params[2];
+
+    dispparams.cArgs = 2;
+    dispparams.cNamedArgs = 0;
+    dispparams.rgdispidNamedArgs = NULL;
+    dispparams.rgvarg = params;
+
+    /* arguments in reverse order: oldPosition, newPosition */
+    V_VT(&params[1]) = VT_R8;
+    V_R8(&params[1]) = old_position;
+    V_VT(&params[0]) = VT_R8;
+    V_R8(&params[0]) = new_position;
+
+    call_sink(wmp->wmpocx, DISPID_WMPCOREEVENT_POSITIONCHANGE, &dispparams);
+}
